# /example/ holds one-to-one artifacts.
#
# Each page under here is built for a single named person, handed to them by
# URL in a message, and linked from nowhere else: not the nav, not index.html,
# not sitemap.xml, not any listing page. It happens to live at a URL. It is not
# part of the site.
#
# robots.txt at the root of this site deliberately allows everything, including
# every AI crawler by name, because the rest of the site WANTS to be found. So
# the noindex has to ride on the response itself. A Disallow line in robots.txt
# would be worse than useless for this directory: it would stop a crawler from
# ever fetching the page, and therefore from ever seeing that it is noindex, so
# a URL discovered some other way could still be indexed. The header below
# applies to every file here, now and later, without anyone remembering to put
# a meta tag in the next one. The pages carry the meta tag as well.
Options -Indexes

<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header set X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet"
</IfModule>
